The One Real Gap That Remains
After reading the README carefully, there is genuinely one gap that is not addressed anywhere:
ECE (Expected Calibration Error) is reported at 0.0671 for the RF model — but no calibration analysis is shown for the full fusion system.
The temperature scaler is applied to the RF model output. But the final soft score combines five models. Whether the final soft score is well-calibrated as a probability is never validated.
This matters because the open-set threshold and friendly threshold are set based on soft score percentiles — if the soft score is poorly calibrated, those thresholds may not generalise.
This is a one-paragraph limitation to acknowledge if asked, not a reason to not present. But be aware of it.





